          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.095,
            0.744,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "Two distinct patterns of stars, the Big Dipper and the Little Dipper, are shown in Fig. 12.4. The **Pole Star** or Polaris, which is part of the Little Dipper is also shown (Fig. 12.4)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.157,
            0.744,
            0.219
          ],
          "content": "The Pole Star appears nearly stationary in the North direction. This helps to locate the North direction in the Northern hemisphere."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.252,
            0.246,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": "Big Dipper"
