          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.485,
            0.272,
            0.74,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": "The Big Dipper lies in the constellation Ursa Major while the Little Dipper lies in the constellation Ursa Minor. In India, the Big Dipper is known as Saptaṛiṣhi, and the Pole Star is known as Dhruva tārā."
        },
